{
  "summary": "This experiment tested the scvi_n200 RNA encoder in a singleprofile setting, achieving validation accuracy of 0.5203 (F1: 0.4982), outperforming the singleprofile baseline (pca_n2000) but lagging behind multiprofile scvi_n200 models. The result suggests the encoder may offer benefits in singleprofile, though its relative impact compared to multiprofile settings remains uncertain. Uncertainty persists about whether encoder performance is profile-agnostic or influenced by aggregation methods, profile complexity, or other untested factors."
}

